    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d833">

                <pb facs="1066" n="964" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg964"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">681.003/144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-02-02T13:00:00+01:00">February 2, 1935—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 2—8:37 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. Embassy’s telegram 31, January 26, noon, and despatch number 941, January
                        31st.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d833-f1"/> Director of African Division informs
                    member of Embassy that French official who was discussing here the question <pb
                        facs="1067" n="965" xml:id="pg965"/> relating to the customs regime in
                    Morocco has returned to Paris after having reached a tentative agreement with
                    the Italian authorities on the subject of the establishment of a system of
                    quotas on certain importations into Morocco as well as on the augmentation of
                    customs duties up to 25 per cent on certain commodities.</p>
                <p>The Italian authorities state that they have insisted that the principles
                    underlying the customs regime in Morocco must be maintained and that any
                    arrangements of a practical nature such as outlined above must be agreed to by
                    all the interested governments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
